speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I have a question for the right hon. the Prime Minister. It arises out of the statement by the Minister of Finance in this house on Thursday, February 8, as reported at page 6514 of Hansard. When answering a question asked by the hon. member for Carleton he commented on a statement made by the chairman of the Economic Council, and the Minister of Finance is reported as having said;
When Mr. Smith made his statement he made it without the knowledge and without the authorization of the government.
My question is this. The Economic Council of Canada was set up by this parliament to be an independent research body. Are we to assume from the minister's statement that this situation is now altered, and that the Economic Council of Canada is only a mouthpiece of the current government and the Minister of Finance?
